<title>USA: Argonaut sees charges, Q3 loss $5.82/shr.</title>
<headline>Argonaut sees charges, Q3 loss $5.82/shr.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In Millions)</p>
<p>				Three Months Ended  Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>				     September 30    September 30</p>
<p>				   1996     1995	1996	1995</p>
<p> Direct Written Premiums$  53.2   $  52.8   $146.4     $141.6</p>
<p> Net Written Premiums	46.8	52.9    137.2	135.3</p>
<p> Earned Premiums	     32.4	52.0    120.9	161.9</p>
<p> Net Investment Income     23.1	24.6     65.8	 76.5</p>
<p>Gain on Sale of Investments</p>
<p>				    0.0	 0.7     21.3	  1.1</p>
<p>	Total Revenue	  55.5	77.3    208.0	239.5</p>
<p>Income (Loss) Before Tax</p>
<p>				(216.3)	11.2  (173.6)	 47.4</p>
<p> Income Tax Provision    (77.0)	 0.9   (64.0)	  7.6</p>
<p>	Net Income (Loss) (139.3)	10.3  (109.6)	 39.8</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss)</p>
<p>    per Common Share     (5.82)	0.43   (4.56)	 1.64</p>
<p>Weighted Average Common</p>
<p>Shares (in thousands)</p>
<p>			     23,928.4  24,170.2  24,037.0  24,341.8</p>
<p>NOTES: The current third quarter and nine-month results include $229 million in charges for increase in loan loss reserves. The figure includes $103 million relating primarily to construction defect claims, asbestos and environmental claims, and claims involving construction of the Los Angeles subway system. Policies construction defects were written for the most part from 1984 through 1990. Environmental claims relate primarily to policies written in the 1970's and early 1980's.  </p>
<p>Additional charges for increased reserves for the quarter include $123 million for unfavorable loss developments under reinsurance contracts assumed in the early- and mid-1970's. The reserve increase mainly covers asbestos and environmental exposure.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
